          "title": "Katie Pizzolato, Vice President, IBM Quantum Platform at IBM Quantum, dispels several quantum computing myths in 60 seconds. She points out that quantum computers are already real and that there are some problems for which quantum computers will probably not be useful."
        },
        {
          "id": "133345142",
          "title": "Director of Research at IBM, Darío Gil, contrasts the main unit of classical information (bit) with the main unit of quantum information (qubit)"
        },
        {
          "id": "134056407",
          "title": "Antonio Corcoles-Gonzales explains superposition and how it relates to probabilistic outcomes of measurements."
        },
        {
          "id": "133345141",
          "title": "Dario Gil describes quantum circuits and the gates that make them up. He motivates the business value of quantum computers by showing the computational states that can be simultaneously realized on a quantum computer."
